A simple student source record
For every external reference, save:

creator or organization;
page, product, project, or file title;
direct URL and access date;
access label and stated licence;
what you learned from it;
what you reused, adapted, or deliberately changed;
what you verified through measurement, testing, or another source.

Do not submit a folder of links as research. Turn sources into evidence, criteria, alternatives, decisions, tests, and an original result.

Fabrication Library & Tools
Use this infrastructure for teacher preparation, advanced work and independent projects:

Free Online Design & Fabrication Resources · Work in Progress: initial research notes for precedents, inclusive design, graphics, CAD, laser cutting, 3D printing, electronics, web design, textiles, CNC, repair, and sustainable fabrication;
Laser Fabrication Library: searchable SVGs, calibration files, palettes, components, holders, jigs and French-cleat concepts;
First Laser Projects Toolkit: worksheet, paper-to-Inkscape support, name-tag files and reference assemblies;
Fabrication Plate Builder: dimensioned plates, holes and layout patterns;
Tool Organizer Gallery: real build evidence, design review and revision status;
Material Fit + Calibration: thickness, scale, kerf, fit and hole tests.

Search the exact title, author or organization. Open the original page or document, not a summary that repeats it. Confirm that the source exists, actually supports the claim, applies to the correct material/tool/context, and is current enough for the decision.
Prefer this order:

local teacher and manufacturer safety instructions;
official standards, government, regulators and original research;
manufacturer documentation for the exact tool/material;
credible technical organizations and experienced practitioners;
secondary explanations used with care.

For dimensions, verify with the real object even when a drawing or product page is available. For images and vectors, record the creator, source URL and licence. “Found online” is not a licence.

